winhttp: keep a WebSocket's connection out of the keep-alive pool, and make blocking receives block.

Forza Horizon 6 (online services: PlayFab lobby, Xbox RTA WebSockets): six threads spun on 'recv error 10035'
(~15000 calls/s each) from the moment the WebSockets opened, until the server reset them.
Base: CrossOver wine sources in work/crossover-source/sources/wine (after patch 0001 and the qh/winhttp header fix).
Apply: cd <wine sources> && patch -p1 < this file; rebuild dlls/winhttp; install in engine + prefix system32.

--- a/dlls/winhttp/winhttp_private.h
+++ b/dlls/winhttp/winhttp_private.h
@@ -121,6 +121,7 @@
     char *peek_msg_mem;
     size_t peek_len;
     HANDLE port;
+    BOOL nonblocking; /* set only while netconn_create or netconn_is_alive poll the socket on purpose */
 };
 
